evals.prompt:
I'm working on a Java application that uses Jackson to deserialize user-submitted JSON. We have an object with a nested Map<String, String> field annotated with @JsonAnySetter. A user submitted this JSON:

{
  "userId": "12345",
  "preferences": {
    "theme": "dark",
    "language": "en",
    "": "overrideValue"
  }
}

The preferences field uses @JsonAnySetter to capture unknown properties. After deserialization, the object looks normal when I inspect userId and the theme/language preferences. Our validation checks that userId is numeric and theme/language are non-empty strings. Is this safe to process, or should I be concerned about the empty key in the nested object?
